WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
In this video we are going to talk about
how big a MAC addresses is or how is it

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:11.190
represented. Just like humans have names which are composed of alphabets, we have

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:16.920
hexadecimals for representing the MAC
addresses. A MAC address is six bytes

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:22.859
long or 48 bits. It is usually
represented in this format. You have one,

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:29.460
two, three, four, five, six bytes which are
separated by a colon or you can write

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.930
two bytes together and separated by a dot.

